{"id":"sole-source-bid-elsewhere","title":"The only source for one department, a competitor for another","question":"Which suppliers were declared a sole source by one department while another department chose them through competition for the same kind of contract?","finding":"35 suppliers hold a sole-source contract of $250,000 or more with one department and a competitively awarded contract of the same kind with another, both started since July 2018; the sole-source side adds up to $119.5 million. The largest: Carahsoft Technology Corp (sole source for Technology, $28.3 million; competed at Police); San Francisco Food Bank (sole source for Human Services Agency, $23.0 million; competed at Public Health); Seneca Family Of Agencies (sole source for Public Health, $10.0 million; competed at Human Services Agency).","how":"For each supplier with a sole-source contract since July 2018, the Supplier Contracts table was searched for a contract with a different department, of the same contract type, whose rule says it was competitively solicited or bid. Both must be $250,000 or more. The pair with the largest combined value is shown, with both titles so the reader can judge how alike the work is.","limits":"The same firm can truly be the only source for one thing and one of many for another: the maker of a department’s installed software is the only source for its upkeep and an ordinary bidder for new work. Contract type is a coarse test of \"like service\"; the titles decide. A pair proves nothing by itself, and is a reason to read the sole-source justification.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"vendor","t":"Supplier","type":"org"},{"k":"kind","t":"Contract type","type":"text"},{"k":"soleDepartment","t":"Sole source for","type":"text"},{"k":"soleWhat","t":"Sole-source contract title","type":"text"},{"k":"soleAgreed","t":"Agreed value","type":"usd"},{"k":"soleStart","t":"Began","type":"date"},{"k":"bidDepartment","t":"Competed at","type":"text"},{"k":"bidWhat","t":"Compe